<input>
project name: quickjs
function signature: JSValue JS_ParseJSON2(JSContext *, const char *, size_t, const char *, int)
</input>

<description>
The function `JS_ParseJSON2` parses a string `buf` of length `buf_len` as a JSON text and returns a `JSValue` representing the parsed value. The `filename` parameter is used for error reporting. The `flags` parameter can be used to enable extensions to the JSON format.
</description>

<requirements>

<requirement>
The `JS_NewRuntime` function should be called to create a `JSRuntime`, and then `JS_NewContext` should be called with the created runtime to get a valid `JSContext *`. This is because the function operates on a JSContext, which must be initialized to a valid state.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `buf` parameter should be a fuzzed byte array, and `buf_len` should be its size. This is because `buf` is the main input to the JSON parser and is user-controlled in all call sites.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `filename` parameter can be a constant string such as "fuzz_input". This is because it is only used for error reporting and does not affect the parsing logic.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `flags` parameter should be either 0 or `JS_PARSE_JSON_EXT` (which is 1). This is because these are the only two values used in the callers of the function.
</requirement>

</requirements>

</function-requirements>

